TITLE='Authentic title "What No One Tells You About Being a Millionaire" is a hidden-truth curiosity frame. The script delivers the promise through a composite (John) and covers inflation, withdrawal income, healthcare, illiquidity, taxes, RMDs, the millionaire profile and hedonic adaptation.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background: the recurring cartoon man, bored expression, holding a cash stack labelled "$1,000,000"; "$1M... NOT RICH?!" in heavy black capitals with an arrow to the cash. At 320x180 the words and the stack read clearly. The thumbnail states the script\'s thesis directly and matches it, although John\'s million is mostly home equity and retirement accounts, not cash.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator story essay built on a composite couple (John and Cara, a teacher and an engineer in their 50s): the anticlimactic moment, inflation-adjusted value, the $2.3M wealthy threshold, 4% rule income, healthcare costs, paper vs spendable wealth, taxes and RMDs, the boring millionaire profile vs a flashy neighbour, investor behaviour, percentile context, the hedonic treadmill, a faceless-YouTube community promotion, and a closing driveway scene. Most numbers reproduce or match sources; the top 10-15% placement, the $700,000 after-tax haircut and the RMD age for John are wrong.'
